  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This recording captures the Mountain Goats performing at the Water Street Music Hall in Rochester, New York, on October 2, 2025 [1]. The audio was captured using Beyerdynamic CK930 and CV900 microphones connected to a Zoom F3 recorder [1]. This specific performance is the 441st of 467 archived shows for the band [2]. The setlist includes twenty-two songs, beginning with “New Britain” and “Corsican Mastiff Stride” [1]. Several tracks are considered rare in the archive, such as “Broken to Begin With” and “Great Pirates” [2]. The performance features notable bustouts, including “Harlem Roulette,” which had not appeared in 37 previous archived shows [2]. “Abide With Me” and “Transjordanian Blues” also returned after long absences from the setlist [2]. The set concludes with “No Children,” which is accompanied by spoken introductions or stories [1]. The full recording runs for 100 minutes and includes an encore [1]. This is the only available recording of this specific date and venue [1].",
